# ============================================================================
# SoyMutDB Portal (apps/web) — Cloudflare Pages redirects
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# SPA fallback: any request that does NOT match a real static file is served
# index.html so client-side (TanStack Router) routes work with a hard reload.
#
# Real static files always win in practice: Pages serves an existing file
# (including SSG HTML such as /about -> about.html and /assets/* hashed
# files) before applying this catch-all — this mirrors Pages' built-in SPA
# behavior when no top-level 404.html exists. Verified post-deploy with:
#   curl -sI https://<site>/about          (expect 200, text/html, NOT index fallback)
#   curl -sI https://<site>/assets/<hash>.js (expect 200, immutable cache)
#
# SSG output (ssg:build + generate-samples): index + 10 content pages +
# 51 sample detail pages + sitemap.xml — none are shadowed by this rule.
# ============================================================================
/* /index.html 200
